  "body": "## Goal\n\nPost one selected closed reentrant DXF perimeter as a vertical opening. Keep the plate outside that perimeter. A separate native job for each opening is sufficient.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nUse an original sketch that has straight lines and circular arcs. Select the loop by identity and preserve its nominal line endpoints, arc centers and winding after placement. Require an internal start with a valid drilled diameter. Verify the complete lead, wire clearance, reentrant corners and retained plate. A sample of the path does not prove clearance.\n\nVerify left compensation on a counterclockwise perimeter or the equivalent verified side for the requested direction. Preserve explicit separation and holding intent. Do not treat an opening as a punch, generate a clearing cycle, or insert a bridge automatically. An unsupported setting must prevent output. The native output must use the guarded zero-step setup in #2984.\n\nUse an independent synthetic job on the offline control. Check formal import, actual placement, the threading position and path direction. Distinguish a geometry check from any effective erosion settings. Do not release a work with unverified steps.\n\n#2022 covers selection of a wire sketch chain. #2983 covers convex tangent punch profiles. #2957 covers openings in a solid model. The chain builder already retains one traversal of an identical reversed straight span and reports the duplicate. See the resolution in #3177. No chain recovery change is required for that case. #3180 adds an explicit selected-chain consumer for straight profiles. This issue needs its exact analytic source and placement for curves. #3179 covers a guarded setup at another height.\n\nSuggested labels: enhancement, P6, effort:max, area:post, area:2d, source:agent.\n",
